e.py`\nImplements `upload_file(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput`. Performs a pre-flight `os.path.exists` check and raises `ValidationError` (exit code 20) immediately if the file is absent. Then initialises `S3Manager`, calls `s3.upload_file(local_file_path, bucket_name, s3_object_key)` → `etag`, computes the S3 URI, updates the `uploaded_s3_uri` OutputField, and returns `ActionOutput(s3_uri=…, etag=…, local_file=…)`.\n\n`/tmp/aws-object-storage/extension-code/src/actions/__init__.py`\nUpdated with explicit imports of `list_objects` and `upload_file`, and `ACTION_MAPPER = {\"List Objects\": list_objects, \"Upload File\": upload_file}`.\n\n**Validation results:** all four files compile cleanly (`py_compile` returned no errors across every `.py` file in `src/`). All imports are absolute and every imported name was confirmed to exist in its source module.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}

